description:
Split of task 123, step 2 of 3. Creates skills/tackle-tasks/task.workflow.js — the single per-task workflow file that replaces the current one-workflow-per-phase layout.

Scope is the dispatcher shell only:
- a `stage` launch argument selecting plan / implement / rebase-test / merge, defaulting to plan+implement when unset;
- meta.name is `task-<N>`, so each concurrent run is separately identifiable;
- phase titles carry the task number (`86 Plan`, `86 Implement`, ...) so six concurrent runs stay distinguishable in /workflows;
- stage bodies are stubs that log and return; nothing calls an agent yet.

The existing skills/tackle-tasks/plan.workflow.js stays untouched here — step 3 moves its planner code across and deletes it. This task and step 3 both edit task.workflow.js, so they are chained: this one must land first.

Read plans/task-86-spec.md (already in the repo) for the full stage plan before writing the dispatcher, even though it is not in this task's files list.

Split of task 124, step 2 of 3. Adds the second half of the review loop to the plan stage of skills/tackle-tasks/task.workflow.js.

Work:
- add a separate `applyFeedback` agent that applies the FIXES block the verify agent (task 134) produced. Splitting review from apply is the point: today skills/tackle-tasks/verify.workflow.js:33-84 has one agent doing both, which lets it rationalize its own review;
- wrap verify + applyFeedback in a loop of up to three rounds;
- after three rounds, proceed to implement regardless of the verdict, and make the objections codex still holds available to the caller so a later task can carry them to the approval gate as proposed tasks;
- move the fix-applying half of verify.workflow.js across and then delete that file — task 134 already moved the reviewing half, so nothing should still import it.

Leave the round counter reachable by step 3: a programmatic missingFiles widening consumes one of the three rounds, so the counter must be decrementable from outside the verify/applyFeedback pair rather than hidden inside the loop body.

This task shares task.workflow.js with tasks 134 and 136 by design; the blockedBy chain keeps them from colliding.

